Contributing to Night Patrol Lookup
Thank you for your interest in contributing to the Night Patrol Lookup System! We welcome bug reports, feature requests, and code contributions.

🚀 Getting Started
Fork the Repository on GitHub.

Clone your fork locally:

git clone https://github.com/your-username/night-patrol-lookup.git
Create a branch for your fix or feature:

git checkout -b feature/amazing-new-feature
🛠️ Development Workflow
Install backend and frontend dependencies in their respective folders:

cd server && npm install
cd ../client && npm install
Ensure existing tests pass and write new tests for added functionality.

Keep code cleanly formatted and linted before committing.

📥 Submitting Pull Requests
Push your changes to your branch:

git push origin feature/amazing-new-feature
Open a Pull Request (PR) against the main branch.

Fill out the PR template completely so reviewers understand your changes.

📜 Code of Conduct
Be respectful, collaborative, and constructive in all discussions, issues, and code reviews.
